As the 2024 first-place winner, I found the experience both professionally and personally rewarding. The competition challenged me to reframe complex economic models into accessible, real-world tools that growers and extension agents could use. It helped me refine my communication skills and reaffirmed my commitment to applied research that addresses agricultural challenges on the ground. Collaborating with my mentor and engaging with other finalists also broadened my perspective on how extension economics can drive innovation and informed decision-making in agriculture. Presenting at the AAEA Annual Meeting and receiving recognition for my work was an invaluable milestone in my academic journey.

